WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.677
It is tempting to think of Spark as simply a larger version of Postgres.

00:00:04.677 --> 00:00:07.172
That is not a good mental model.

00:00:07.172 --> 00:00:09.787
Postgres is a database system.

00:00:09.787 --> 00:00:18.082
It is designed to store and manage relational data, support transactions, enforce constraints, use indexes,

00:00:18.082 --> 00:00:20.640
and answer database queries efficiently.

00:00:21.159 --> 00:00:24.316
Spark is mainly a distributed computing engine.

00:00:24.316 --> 00:00:31.711
Its strength is processing large analytical workloads by spreading work across multiple machines or workers.

00:00:31.711 --> 00:00:35.876
In a real organization, these tools can work together.

00:00:35.876 --> 00:00:42.656
A database may manage operational data, while Spark prepares large analytical datasets.

00:00:42.656 --> 00:00:45.996
The question is not which tool is better in general.

00:00:45.996 --> 00:00:48.746
The question is which tool fits the workload.
